This implementation ensures that large arrays are handled efficiently by processing them asynchronously and one-by-one to prevent blocking the event loop for a long time. It also includes error handling both at the higher level (if the argument is not an array, or if reducer is not a function) and within the callback execution itself (to handle errors during the reduction process).

