```php
class PasswordManager {
    private $hashedPassword;
    private $saltRounds = 12;

    public function generateRandomString($length) {
        // Define the character set
        $characters = '0123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ';

        // Generate a random string from the character set
        $randomString = '';
        for ($i = 0; $i < $length; $i++) {
            $index = mt_rand(0, strlen($characters) - 1);
            $randomString .= $characters[$index];
        }

        return $randomString;
    }

    public function hashPassword($password) {
        // Hash the password using bcrypt with the set salt round count
        $this->hashedPassword = password_hash($password, PASSWORD_BCRYPT, ['cost' => $this->saltRounds]);

        return $this->hashedPassword;
    }

    public function checkPassword($password) {
        // Check if the given password matches the hashed password
        if (password_verify($password, $this->hashedPassword)) {
            return true;
        } else {
            return false;
        }
    }

    public function validateCharacterSet($characterSet) {
        // Check if the character set contains at least one uppercase letter, 
        // one lowercase letter, one digit, and one special character
        $uppercase = preg_match('@[A-Z]@', $characterSet);
        $lowercase = preg_match('@[a-z]@', $characterSet);
        $number    = preg_match('@[0-9]@', $characterSet);

        if(!$uppercase || !$lowercase || !$number) {
            return false;
        } else {
            return true;
        }
    }

    public function setSaltRoundCount($rounds) {
        // Set the salt round count for bcrypt hashing algorithm
        $this->saltRounds = $rounds;
    }

    public function resetPassword() {
        // Generate a new random string with the length of 8 characters and hash it
        $newRandomString = $this->generateRandomString(8);
        $hashedPassword = $this->hashPassword($newRandomString);

        return $hashedPassword;
    }
}
```
The PasswordManager class provides a set of methods to handle password related operations. It includes the ability to generate random strings, hash passwords using bcrypt algorithm and validate character sets. The hashed password can be checked against the original inputted password. There're also options to change the salt rounds count used in bcrypt. Lastly, there is a method that resets the stored password to a new one generated with the current settings.

