Here is a basic example to illustrate what you asked for in Java. The `find` method of UnionFind class is used to check disjointness by comparing parents of elements in pairs:

```java
import java.util.*;

class UnionFind {
    private int[] parent; 
    private byte[] rank;

    public UnionFind(int size) {
        if (size < 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException();
        parent = new int[size];
        rank = new byte[size];
        for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {
            parent[i] = i;
            rank[i] = 0;
        }
    }

    public int find(int p) {
        while (p != parent[p]) {
            parent[p] = parent[parent[p]];  
            p = parent[p];
        }
        return p;
    }

    public void union(int p, int q) {
        int rootP = find(p);
        int rootQ = find(q);
        if (rootP == rootQ) return;

        if      (rank[rootP] < rank[rootQ]) parent[rootP] = rootQ;
        else if (rank[rootP] > rank[rootQ]) parent[rootQ] = rootP;
        else {
            parent[rootQ] = rootP;
            rank[rootP]++;
        }
    }
}

public class Main {

    public static int countDisjointPairs(int[] array, UnionFind uf) {
        if (array == null || array.length <= 1) return 0;

        int disjointCount = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < array.length - 1; i++) {
            long start = System.currentTimeMillis();

            uf.union(array[i], array[i+1]);

            if (uf.find(array[i]) != uf.find(array[i + 1])) disjointCount++; 

            long end = System.currentTimeMillis();
            System.out.println("Time taken for pair (" + array[i] + ", " + array[i+1] + ") in milliseconds: " + (end - start));
        }

        return disjointCount;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] array = new int[]{0, 1, 2, 3, 4}; // example input
        UnionFind uf = new UnionFind(array.length);

        System.out.println("Number of disjoint pairs: " + countDisjointPairs(array, uf));
    }
}
```
This code will only provide a rough estimate for the time taken per pair as it calculates time before and after union operation. To get exact duration of union operation you would have to do `System.currentTimeMillis()` before calling union and subtract start time from that value.

