Here is a simplified implementation in JavaScript using Node.js APIs for buffers. This function does not handle multiple sources or file handling as requested. The implementation only supports one buffer at the moment:

```javascript
/**
 * Copy data from a specified range within a source buffer into a new buffer. 
 * @param {ArrayBuffer} source - Source array buffer containing the data to be copied.
 * @param {number} start - Index in the source buffer where copying should start.
 * @param {number} length - Number of bytes to copy from the source buffer.
 * @return {ArrayBuffer} Newly created buffer with the copied data. 
 */
function copyData(source, start, length) {
    // Ensure start and end positions are within bounds of source buffer
    if (start < 0 || length < 1 || (start + length) > source.byteLength) throw 'Invalid byte range';

    let sourceView = new Uint8Array(source);
    let targetBuffer = new ArrayBuffer(length); // Create a new array buffer to hold the copied data
    let targetView = new Uint8Array(targetBuffer); 

    for (let i = 0; i < length; i++) { // Directly copy bytes into new buffer, bypassing Array.prototype.slice() for better performance
        targetView[i] = sourceView[start + i]; 
    }

    return targetBuffer;
}
```

