Here is an example of how you could implement such a function in C. This example assumes that `log_structure_creation` and `NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T` are properly defined, and you have a way to validate if a given structure meets the predefined rules in the JSON file.

Please note that this implementation doesn't handle dynamic changes to the CRC flag rules without recompiling the code because that requires a more complex approach like using callback functions or signals/slots mechanism which are specific to the operating system and language you're using, so it might not be applicable for all cases.

```c
#include <stdlib.h> // malloc, free, rand
#include <pthread.h> // pthread_mutex_*
#include <jansson.h> // json_load_file, json_object_*

extern int log_structure_creation(NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T *);
extern int validate_rules(NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T *);

pthread_mutex_t mutex = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;

int generateNfalist(int num_structures, NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T **nfalist, const char *rules_config_file) {
    pthread_mutex_lock(&mutex); // Lock the mutex to ensure thread safety.

    *nfalist = malloc(num_structures * sizeof(NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T));
    if (*nfalist == NULL) {
        pthread_mutex_unlock(&mutex); // Unlock the mutex in case of error.
        return -1;
    }

    json_error_t error;
    json_t *rules = json_load_file(rules_config_file, 0, &error);
    if (rules == NULL) {
        free(*nfalist); // Free allocated memory in case of error.
        pthread_mutex_unlock(&mutex); // Unlock the mutex in case of error.
        return -1;
    }

    for (int i = 0; i < num_structures; ++i) {
        NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T *structure = &(*nfalist)[i];

        // Populate structure.
        structure->RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG = 123;  // You can set unique values or generate them randomly.
        structure->RNTI = rand();  // Generate a random RNTI.

        json_t *rule = json_object_get(rules, structure->RNTI);
        if (json_is_boolean(rule)) {
            structure->CRC_INDICATION_REL8_TAG.CRCFLAG = json_boolean_value(rule);
        } else {
            // Handle error: JSON doesn't contain a boolean value for the RNTI.
        }

        if (!validate_rules(structure)) {
            // Handle error: Structure does not meet the rules.
        }

        log_structure_creation(structure);
    }

    json_decref(rules);
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&mutex); // Unlock the mutex after all operations are done.
    return 0;
}
```
This code doesn't handle error checking for `validate_rules` or `log_structure_creation` functions because it depends on their implementation, but in a real-world scenario you should add appropriate checks to make sure these functions do not fail unexpectedly. Also note that this function assumes the structure of your JSON file to be a simple object where each key is an RNTI and its value is a boolean indicating whether CRC flag should be set. If it has a different structure, adjust the code accordingly.

