Below is an outline of how one might approach this problem in Java using JSch for SSH connections and Docker-java for container deployment. This code is intended to be a starting point and would require further development and fine-tuning based on the exact requirements. 

```Java
import com.jcraft.jsch.*;
import org.apache.commons.lang3.StringUtils;
import com.github.dockerjava.api.DockerClient;
import com.github.dockerjava.core.DefaultDockerClientConfig;
import com.github.dockerjava.core.DockerClientBuilder;
import com.github.dockerjava.api.command.CreateContainerResponse;
import org.slf4j.*;
import java.util.Properties;
import java.io.*;
import java.net.*;

public class DynamicServerDiscovery {
    private static final Logger logger = LoggerFactory.getLogger(DynamicServerDiscovery.class);
    private JSch jsch = new JSch();
    private Session session;

    public void discoverServers() throws IOException, JSchException {
        // Fetch server details from properties file or any other source and store them in a List of Server objects

        for (Server server : servers) {
            connectToServer(server);

            // Deploy container to discovered server
            deployContainer(server.getDockerHost());

            disconnectFromServer();
        }
    }

    private void connectToServer(Server server) throws JSchException {
        session = jsch.getSession(server.getUser(), server.getIp(), 22);
        session.setPassword(server.getPassword());

        // Avoid known hosts checking for simplicity in this example
        Properties config = new java.util.Properties();
        config.put("StrictHostKeyChecking", "no");
        session.setConfig(config);

        session.connect();
    }

    private void deployContainer(String dockerHost) {
        DockerClient dockerClient = DockerClientBuilder.getInstance(DefaultDockerClientConfig.createDefaultConfigBuilder()
            .withDockerHost(dockerHost)
            .build()).build();

        CreateContainerResponse container = 
                dockerClient.createContainerCmd("container_image")
                    .withName("container_name")
                    .exec();

        dockerClient.startContainerCmd(container.getId()).exec();
    }

    private void disconnectFromServer() {
        if (session != null) {
            session.disconnect();
        }
    }
}
```

This code will discover servers based on details fetched from a properties file or any other source, connect to each server via SSH and then deploy a container image using Docker Java API. 

