Here is a Java code snippet to solve the problem with the features mentioned in question:

```java
import java.util.*;
import org.apache.http.client.methods.*;
import org.apache.http.entity.*;
import org.apache.http.impl.client.*;
import com.google.gson.*;
import java.io.IOException;

class Node {
    int rank, parent;

    public Node(int p) {
        this.rank = 0;
        this.parent = p;
    }
}

class UnionFind {
    private static Map<Integer, Node> map = new HashMap<>();

    public static void makeSet(int[] arr) {
        for (int i : arr)
            map.put(i, new Node(i));
    }

    public static int find(int x) {
        if (map.get(x).parent != x)
            map.get(x).parent = find(map.get(x).parent);

        return map.get(x).parent;
    }

    public static void union(int x, int y) {
        int xRoot = find(x), yRoot = find(y);

        if (xRoot == yRoot)
            return;

        if (map.get(xRoot).rank < map.get(yRoot).rank)
            map.get(xRoot).parent = yRoot;

        else if (map.get(xRoot).rank > map.get(yRoot).rank)
            map.get(yRoot).parent = xRoot;

        else {
            map.get(yRoot).parent = xRoot;
            int rank = map.get(xRoot).rank;
            map.put(xRoot, new Node(++rank));
        }
    }
}

class ErrorHandler {
   public static void handleError(String error) {
      System.out.println("ERROR: " + error);
   }
}

class APICommunicator {
   private static final String endpoint = "http://example.com/api";

   public static void logData(int pairsCount, long timeTaken) throws IOException {
      HttpPost postRequest = new HttpPost(endpoint);

      Map<String, Integer> dataMap = new HashMap<>();
      dataMap.put("pairsCount", pairsCount);
      dataMap.put("timeTaken", (int) timeTaken);

      StringEntity payload = new StringEntity(new Gson().toJson(dataMap));
      postRequest.setEntity(payload);
      postRequest.setHeader("Content-type", "application/json");

      CloseableHttpClient httpClient = HttpClients.createDefault();
      httpClient.execute(postRequest);
   }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException{
        int arr[] = {1, 2, 3, 4}; // example array

        UnionFind.makeSet(arr);
        int pairsCount = 0;

        long startTime = System.currentTimeMillis();
        for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; ++i) {
            for (int j = i + 1; j < arr.length; ++j) {
                if (UnionFind.find(arr[i]) != UnionFind.find(arr[j])){
                    pairsCount++;
                }
                UnionFind.union(arr[i], arr[j]);
            }
        }
        long timeTaken = System.currentTimeMillis() - startTime;

        APICommunicator.logData(pairsCount, timeTaken);
    }
}
```
In the code above, UnionFind class is responsible for maintaining disjoint sets and performing find operations on them using path compression technique to optimize union by rank. 
The error handling is done in a separate utility class ErrorHandler which logs the errors with their descriptions. 
APICommunicator class communicates with an external API endpoint to log data using HTTP POST request. The payload contains the number of disjoint pairs found and the time taken for the operation.
