```javascript
function asyncStreamReducer(stream) {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    const result = []; // Array to store results from the stream

    // Function to handle data from the stream
    const processData = (data) => {
      if (typeof data !== 'number') {
        throw new Error('Invalid data. Expected number');
      } else {
        result.push(data);
      }
    };

    // Event handlers for the stream events
    stream.on('data', processData);
    stream.on('error', reject);
    stream.on('end', () => {
      // Clean up event listeners to prevent memory leaks
      stream.removeListener('data', processData);
      stream.removeListener('error', reject);

      resolve(result);
    });
  });
}
```
To use this function, you would pass a readable stream (like a file stream, http response stream etc) to it. The function returns a promise that resolves with the array of numbers from the stream when the stream ends or rejects with an error if there's an issue reading from the stream. 

