To implement this service we will use Spring Boot framework and the Spring Async feature to perform file reading asynchronously. Here is a basic skeleton of such service class:

```java
import java.io.File;
import java.io.IOException;
import java.nio.file.Files;
import java.security.MessageDigest;
import java.security.NoSuchAlgorithmException;
import java.util.concurrent.CompletableFuture;

import org.apache.commons.codec.binary.Hex;
import org.springframework.scheduling.annotation.Async;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;
import org.slf4j.Logger;
import org.slf4j.LoggerFactory;

@Service
public class Md5HashService {
    private static final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(Md5HashService.class);

    @Async("fileReadExecutor")
    public CompletableFuture<String> calculateMD5Async(String filePath) throws IOException, NoSuchAlgorithmException {
        File file = new File(filePath);

        if (!file.exists() || !file.isFile()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("The provided path does not point to a valid file.");
        }

        MessageDigest md5Digest = MessageDigest.getInstance("MD5");

        Files.readAllBytes(file.toPath()).forEach(md5Digest::update);

        return CompletableFuture.completedFuture(new String(Hex.encodeHex(md5Digest.digest())));
    }
}
```

The `calculateMD5Async` method takes a file path, validates it and then reads the file in an asynchronous manner. If the provided path is not valid or reading the file fails for any reason, an appropriate exception is thrown. 

To make this service integrate into Spring Boot application, ensure your main Spring Boot Application class has `@EnableAsync` annotation and `@Configuration` for async support and also a custom Executor bean:

```java
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Bean;
import org.springframework.scheduling.concurrent.ThreadPoolTaskExecutor;

@SpringBootApplication
@EnableAsync
public class Application {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SpringApplication.run(Application.class, args);
    }

    @Bean("fileReadExecutor")
    public Executor taskExecutor() {
        ThreadPoolTaskExecutor executor = new ThreadPoolTaskExecutor();
        executor.setCorePoolSize(4);
        executor.setMaxPoolSize(10);
        executor.setQueueCapacity(50);
        executor.setThreadNamePrefix("fileRead-");
        executor.initialize();
        return executor;
    }
}
```

This will allow Spring to run the `calculateMD5Async` method in a separate thread pool, improving performance and responsiveness when dealing with large files.

In terms of error handling, we have added validation checks at the start of our method to ensure that the provided path is valid. If it isn't, an `IllegalArgumentException` will be thrown with an appropriate message. Other unforeseen exceptions are also caught and re-thrown as generic RuntimeExceptions so they can be handled by other parts of your application or framework if necessary.

