public class DistributedSessionCacheManager {
    private final ConcurrentHashMap<String, Session> cache;
    private final int MAX_CACHE_SIZE;

    public DistributedSessionCacheManager(int maxSize) {
        this.MAX_CACHE_SIZE = maxSize;
        this.cache = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    }

    // Maintain LRU cache by removing the eldest entry if we go over the size limit
    public void put(String sessionId, Session session) {
        cache.putIfAbsent(sessionId, session);
        if (cache.size() > MAX_CACHE_SIZE) {
            Optional<Map.Entry<String, Session>> eldest = cache.entrySet().stream()
                    .min(Comparator.comparingLong(e -> e.getValue().getLastAccessed()));
            eldest.ifPresent(sessionIdToSessionEntry -> cache.remove(sessionIdToSessionEntry.getKey()));
        }
    }

    public Session getIfPresent(String sessionId) {
        return cache.get(sessionId);
    }
}
``` 
This is a very simplified version and doesn't include the additional aspects like session conflicts management, logging, alerting, dynamic cache size adjustment or handling of group sessions. Moreover, it assumes a Session class already exists that has methods for getting last accessed timestamp and other necessary details. In reality, each of these would be their own classes or perhaps interfaces which could be implemented in different ways depending on the specific requirements of your application.

